<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine banks function normally despite strike.</title>
<headline>Argentine banks function normally despite strike.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1996-12-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentine banks were working normally Thursday in spite of a general strike by unions protesting the government's labor reforms, the banks' association said.</p>
<p>A spokesman for the Association of Argentine Banks (ADEBA) said all banks have taken the necessary steps to ensure that full services will be provided.</p>
<p>The walkout, the third general strike this year, was called by unions to protest three decrees on labor market reforms signed by President Carlos Menem last week. Unlike the other strikes however, no marches or protests were called for this time.</p>
<p>((-- Buenos Aires Newsroom, 541 318-0668))</p>
